<h3>Pins show the neighborhood, not the door</h3>
<p>8bit.nyc is a pixel art map, drawn for fun and for a quick look at what is happening around the city. Every pin marks the approximate location of an event, so think of it as pointing to the right part of town rather than the exact building, entrance or room. Streets, parks, landmarks and buildings are drawn to look like New York, not to match it block for block.</p>

<h3>Check the details before you go</h3>
<p>Listings are collected automatically from outside sources such as public calendars, ticketing sites and venues' own pages. Dates, times, prices, addresses and line-ups can change or be wrong, and events can be cancelled. Always confirm with the event's own page or the organizer before you head out.</p>

<h3>Subway, airports, weather and parking</h3>
<p>Subway alerts, airport security wait times, the weather and the alternate side parking calendar come from the MTA, the Port Authority of New York and New Jersey, the National Weather Service and NYC DOT. We are not affiliated with or endorsed by any of them. This information can be delayed or incomplete, and the subway lines are drawn roughly where they run. For travel, flights, parking and safety decisions, rely on the official sources linked in each panel and leave yourself extra time at the airport.</p>

<h3>No endorsement</h3>
<p>The characters on the map are pixel art made for fun and are not connected with, or endorsed by, any person or company. If you think something we drew is yours, or is you, and you would like it changed or removed, email info@8bit.nyc and we will look at it promptly. Showing an event, venue or organizer on the map does not mean we recommend or vouch for it. 8bit.nyc is provided as is, without warranties of any kind, and we are not responsible for any loss or inconvenience that comes from relying on it. See our <a href="#terms" data-modal="terms">Terms and Conditions</a> for the full terms.</p>
